+### 3.1 The same gates on Linux
+
+A second operating system, on the same machine: Ubuntu 24.04 under WSL 2, Python 3.12.3 with numpy 1.26.4 and Pillow 12.3.0, Rust 1.98.0, gcc. The repository was cloned at `6d547d0`, and the six released fixtures were copied in and checked against their pins (`fetch_fixtures.py --check`: all verified). Source S14.
+
+| gate | Linux at `6d547d0` | Windows at `6d547d0` |
+|---|---|---|
+| `cargo test` (core) | 44 passed | 44 passed |
+| Stage 2, `run_gate.py` | 11 PASS, 0 FAIL, 0 SKIP | 11 PASS |
+| Gate A | 10 PASS, 0 FAIL, 0 SKIP | 10 PASS |
+| Gate 6 | 23 PASS, 0 FAIL, 1 SKIP | 23 PASS, 1 SKIP |
+| Gate 9 | 14 PASS, 0 FAIL, 1 SKIP | 14 PASS, 1 SKIP |
+| Gate 12 | 16 PASS, 1 FAIL, 1 SKIP (the rebuild clause needs a private path; fixed in #6) | 16 PASS, 1 FAIL, 1 SKIP |
+| CC0 public / image / gsplat | 14 / 9 / 8 PASS, 0 FAIL | 14 / 9 / 8 PASS |
+| Store suite | 58 passed, 1 skipped | 58 passed, 1 skipped |
+
+Every gate gives the same result on both systems. Gate 3B, Blender and Unreal were not run on Linux.
+
+Two observations, neither a gate failure:
+
+- **Last-digit floats.** Values computed through the C maths library can differ in the last digit between Linux (glibc) and Windows (MSVC). A rebuild of `ista-varun-v1` on Linux differs from the pin only in `semantics/semantics.json` (largest relative difference 1.7e-16). #6 handles this case.
+- **`humanoid-retarget-v1.werk` does not rebuild byte for byte.** Gate 6 builds it when the file is missing. Builds on Windows (1 510 605 B) and Linux (1 510 598 B) both differ from the pin (1 514 545 B). The walk clip differs from the pin in the last digits of its floats, the fit results differ between the two systems the same way, and `x/retarget-report.json` embeds the absolute path of the build machine. The gate's tolerances (1e-9 and wider) are not affected.
+
